Package: pmatools
Title: Pairwise Meta-Analysis with Certainty Ratings Following the Core
    GRADE Series
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Yuki", "Furukawa", email = "furukawa.y.psy@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: End-to-end pairwise meta-analysis pipeline with certainty
    ratings following the Core GRADE series, Summary of Findings table,
    and reproducible export bundle. pmatools implements the Core GRADE
    series (Guyatt et al., BMJ 2025), which summarizes GRADE guidance;
    it is not an official GRADE Working Group tool.
    Wraps the {meta} package for data ingestion (long/wide), random- or
    common-effect pooling, contour-enhanced funnel plots with Egger's test,
    and auto-laid-out forest plots. Certainty ratings follow the BMJ 2025
    Core GRADE series (Guyatt et al.): Risk of Bias (BMJ Fig 2 weight-based
    dominance plus inflation threshold), Inconsistency (BMJ Fig 2 flowchart
    with a clinical decision Threshold), Indirectness (manual), Imprecision
    (CI vs Threshold + Optimal Information Size from Threshold), and Publication Bias
    (Egger / unpublished-studies flowchart). Outputs SoF flextable, multi-
    outcome evidence-profile table, and Appendix report (docx/html/pdf/md),
    and bundles everything plus a reproducible analysis.R into a ZIP archive.
